4. Evaluation Design

4.1 Test 1: Bottleneck Identification Accuracy

Protocol. Sample size: 50–100 cases. Expert panel: 3 blinded expert caseworkers with \geq 5 years experience. Each panelist independently ranks the top 3 bottlenecks for each case. Primary outcome: top-1 agreement between AI and panel majority. Secondary outcome: Spearman rank correlation across top 3.

Thresholds. Top-1 agreement \geq 70\%. Spearman rank correlation \geq 0.6. False bottleneck rate (bottlenecks judged irrelevant or harmful) < 5\%. Inter-rater reliability reported using Fleiss' \kappa.

4.2 Test 2: Time-to-Stabilization

Protocol. Design: stepped-wedge cluster randomized trial. The number of clusters N_{\text{clusters}} is determined prospectively by

N_{\text{clusters}} = f(\text{effect size}, \text{ICC}, \text{power}, \alpha, \text{attrition}, \text{design}),

rather than fixed a priori. Primary outcome: time from first contact to stable housing (30 consecutive days in permanent housing). Analysis: survival models with intention-to-treat and site-level random effects.

Threshold. 15\% reduction in time-to-stabilization, with p < 0.05.

4.3 Test 3: Trajectory Durability

Protocol. Sample: all individuals who stabilized in Test 2. Primary outcome: return to homelessness within 12 months. Analysis: logistic regression with site fixed effects and adjustment for baseline risk.

Threshold. 10 percentage point reduction in 12-month return rate, with p < 0.05, defined as the Minimum Important Difference (MID).

4.4 Test 4: Dignity, Consent, and Autonomy

Protocol. Mixed methods. Quantitative: validated scales for autonomy, trust, and perceived surveillance. Qualitative: semi-structured interviews with 20 participants, including opt-outs. Instrument pre-registered before data collection.

Thresholds. No more than 10\% of users report feeling surveilled, judged, or coerced. Median autonomy subscale at or above midpoint.

4.5 Phased Evaluation

· Phase A — Expert validation. N \approx 50\text{--}100.
· Phase B — Prospective observational pilot. N \approx 200\text{--}500.
· Phase C — Cluster randomized evaluation. Dimensioned statistically via prospective power analysis.

This creates a progression: proof of concept \to pilot \to effectiveness.

4.6 Process Metrics

Metric Definition Target
Time from first message to first referral Elapsed time < 48 hours
Referral completion rate % referrals closed with tracked outcome 60%
Resource data staleness Median age relative to resource-specific TTL Within TTL
False bottleneck rate Bottlenecks judged irrelevant or harmful < 5\%
