We define the belief update operator \tau: given belief b, action a, and observation y,

\tau(b,a,y)(x') = \frac{O(y\mid x')\sum_x P(x'\mid x,a)b(x)}{\sum_{x''}O(y\mid x'')\sum_x P(x''\mid x,a)b(x)},

with predicted observation probability

P(y\mid b,a) = \sum_{x''}O(y\mid x'')\sum_x P(x''\mid x,a)b(x).

We write N_y(b)(x') = O(y\mid x')\sum_x P(x'\mid x,a)b(x) for the unnormalized numerator; N_y(b) is linear in b.

