E.3 Consent Token Format

The consent token is a signed, verifiable credential with the following fields:

· subject_id (pseudonymous identifier)
· scope (set of permitted data uses)
· issued_at, expires_at
· issuer (CoC or authorized party)
· signature (over the above fields)

Withdrawal (STOP) triggers revocation of the token and deletion of the associated operational case data within a defined retention window.

E.4 SMS / Voice Interface

Supported keywords:

· START: initiate consent.
· STOP: withdraw consent, delete operational case data.
· HELP: request assistance from a human caseworker.
· STATUS: check referral status.
· NEXT: request next recommendation.
· EXPLAIN: request plain-language explanation.
· VETO: reject current recommendation.

Voice interface supports natural language input via speech-to-text, text-to-speech output, and consent capture via voice signature.

