E.6 Resource-Specific TTL Function

For each resource r, the TTL is

\mathrm{TTL}_r = f(\text{type}_r, \text{volatility}_r, \text{capacity}_r, \text{risk}_r).

Illustrative values:

· Emergency shelter bed: 15 minutes.
· Food bank capacity: 24 hours.
· Training program enrollment: 7 days.
· Permanent housing unit: 48 hours.

These values are proposed defaults, subject to calibration with local service providers.

E.7 Deployment Topology

The system is deployed as a federated architecture with:

· A central secure aggregation server.
· Regional HLN instances colocated with CoCs.
· Local adapters for HMIS, Coordinated Entry, HSDS, and closed-loop referral networks.
· Provider-agnostic access gateways (SMS, voice, mobile, web).
· Nonprofit governance with community advisory board oversight.

